The U.K.&#x2019;s harassment and bullying watchdog has seen a spike in whistleblowing reports following Russell Brand &#x2019;s conviction for rape earlier this month.

Creative Industries Independent Standards Authority, a voluntary body with support across media and the arts, has said it received over 90 reports since launching its whistleblowing service in June, with a spike following Brand&#x2019;s conviction. Related Stories Netflix Closes $380 Million Acquisition of Radford Studio Center Netflix Orders Harlan Coben Limited Series 'The Innocent' From 'I Will Find You' Team

The former comedian was sentenced to 10 and a half years in prison after a jury found him guilty of one count of rape and three counts of sexual assault. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

The reports cover all the sectors represented by CIISA including film, tv, music, theatre and live performance.

CIISA is an officially designated whistleblowing body and its confidential whistleblowing service is available for those in need of immediate support while enabling it to build up insight. Reports will be used to identify patterns and issues which it can then report back to policymakers and to the industry.

Where necessary, the body will also make &#x201C;lawful referrals.&#x201D;

The news comes as CIISA hosted an event in Parliament Wednesday to engage industry leaders and lawmakers on preventing harmful behaviour in the creative industries. It was hosted by CIISA chair Baroness Helena Kennedy with attendees including numerous MPs, including chair of the digital, culture, media and sport committee Caroline Dinenage as well as media figures such as BBC chair Samir Shah and ex-BBC director general Tim Davie.

The event marked the official launch of CIISA&#x2019;s register, which displays the organizations financially contributing to CIISA. Orgs supporting the watchdog will be entitled to carry a CIISA registration mark, demonstrating their commitment to the body&#x2019;s standards, as well as access to events and resources. Contributions are made on a financial sliding scale, with no company expected to pay more than 0.1% of its U.K. turnover. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

"CIISA has a pivotal role to play in preventing harm and closing accountability gaps in the creative industry infrastructure, offering a unique opportunity to identify harmful patterns of behaviour across different projects,&#x201D; said CIISA CEO Jen Smith.

&#x201C;We thank the organisations who have already pledged their support for this important work and we will continue to work alongside industry and Government to ensure that CIISA is adequately resourced to offer a safe, confidential route for people to seek independent advice and report concerns, and to embed the consistent cross-sector standards that will drive lasting change.&#x201D;

The Hollywood Reporter announced Wednesday that award-winning writer, director, actor and producer Mindy Kaling will receive this year&#x2019;s Equity in Entertainment Award during its annual Women in Entertainment breakfast gala in Los Angeles.

Actor Maitreyi Ramakrishnan, who starred in Kaling&#x2019;s hit Netflix series Never Have I Ever , will present Kaling with the award. Kaling joins Taylor Swift, who The Hollywood Reporter previously announced will receive the Sherry Lansing Leadership Award, as an honoree at this year&#x2019;s gala. Related Stories General News Taylor Swift Will Be Honored With The Hollywood Reporter's Sherry Lansing Leadership Award at Women in Entertainment Gala News Black Lives Matter Activist DeRay Mckesson Talks Losing Key Trump-Era Protest Mobilization Tool: "I Miss Twitter"

Additionally, actress and comedian Mary Beth Barone is set to open the program, which is presented by founding sponsor Lifetime and title sponsor Lilly. Lina Polimeni, chief marketing officer &#x2014; consumer at Eli Lilly and Company, will share remarks on the important intersection of health and entertainment. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4],[300,251]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

The Equity in Entertainment Award recognizes individuals who amplify the voices of underrepresented communities in the entertainment industry. The award was created in 2016, and previous honorees include Jennifer Lopez, Selena Gomez, Kerry Washington, Issa Rae, Ryan Murphy, Amy Pascal and Nina Jacobson.

&#x201C;Mindy Kaling is one of the most influential creative voices of her generation," said Maer Roshan, editor-in-chief of The Hollywood Reporter. "Through her sharp humor, emotional honesty and inclusive storytelling, Kaling creates opportunities for new perspectives and stories to take center stage. We&#x2019;re thrilled to recognize her with this year&#x2019;s Equity in Entertainment Award, celebrating her enduring contributions to the industry and her commitment to making entertainment more inclusive and reflective of the world we live in.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Kaling is an Emmy-nominated writer, Tony Award-winning producer, New York Times best-selling author, acclaimed director and actor. At age 24, Kaling joined the writing staff of NBC&#x2019;s The Office , becoming the only woman on the team. She penned 23 episodes over eight seasons, which was more than any other writer. Kaling also earned an Emmy nomination, marking the first time a woman of color had been recognized in any writing category.

Her achievements have continued to garner national recognition. In 2023, Kaling was awarded the National Medal of Arts by the White House, the highest honor bestowed upon artists by the U.S. government, and received the Producers Guild of America&#x2019;s Norman Lear Achievement Award in Television. She has been named to Time &#x2019;s 100 Most Influential People in the World list (2012), and in 2022, her company, Kaling International, was named one of Time&#x2019; s 100 Most Influential Companies.

Kaling is the creator, star and executive producer of the hit series The Mindy Project , for which she wrote 24 of the show&#x2019;s 117 episodes over six celebrated seasons. Since then, she has solidified her reputation as one of Hollywood&#x2019;s most prolific and powerful storytellers, particularly in shaping the future of comedy, teen drama and women-led television.

In 2020, she created the Netflix teen dramedy Never Have I Ever , which reached 40 million households in its first four weeks and concluded in 2023 to widespread acclaim. She co-created and executive produced The Sex Lives of College Girls , which became the most watched comedy premiere on Max in 2021. In 2024, she produced the Oscar-nominated short film Anuja , a powerful narrative about sisterhood, exploitation and hope. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-thr-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setLazyLoadMultiplier(2) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

In 2025, Kaling co-created and executive produced Running Point for Netflix, which debuted as the No. 1 TV show in the U.S., surpassing a billion minutes viewed in its first week. The series was quickly renewed for a second season, which recently premiered on Netflix. She is also the creator and executive producer of the 2026 Hulu series Not Suitable for Work , a workplace dramedy following a group of ambitious young professionals in Manhattan.

Through her company, Kaling International, she has cultivated a distinctive brand rooted in sharp humor, emotional honesty and inclusive storytelling. Her leadership has helped launch the careers of diverse new writers, showrunners and creatives, particularly women and people of color who have gone on to shape major projects across the industry.

Beyond television and film, Kaling is a best-selling author. Her comedic memoirs Is Everyone Hanging Out Without Me? (And Other Concerns) and Why Not Me? became New York Times best-sellers, followed by her personal essay collection Nothing Like I Imagined . She went on to launch Mindy&#x2019;s Book Studio in partnership with Amazon Publishing, an imprint dedicated to championing new and underrepresented literary voices. In January 2027, Kaling will release I Did Everything Right, Right? , a collection of six personal essays from Amazon Original Stories exploring motherhood, ambition, identity and the unexpected realities of adulthood with her signature wit and candor.

Polimeni will speak about the need for more accurate depictions of breast cancer onscreen. She will cite research, funded by Lilly and conducted with Dr. Stacy Smith and the USC Annenberg Inclusion Initiative, finding that just two female characters had breast cancer across a full year of Hollywood&#x2019;s most popular films and TV shows, out of more than 8,600 speaking characters. Polimeni will urge the industry to bring more stories to screen that reflect the experiences of women living with breast cancer. Her remarks come as Lilly brings free mobile mammograms to Koreatown in Los Angeles from Dec. 4-6, a neighborhood with one of the densest concentrations of late-stage breast cancer diagnoses in L.A. County, so more women can get screened close to home. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-thr-article-mid-articleX-uid3' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setLazyLoadMultiplier(2) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Ramakrishnan first captured the attention of international audiences as the charmingly relatable Devi Vishwakumar in Netflix&#x2019;s hit series Never Have I Ever and has shifted into high gear ever since. She leads Netflix&#x2019;s comedy dance film Best of the Best , now streaming. Other recent projects include scene-stealing as Lindsay Lohan&#x2019;s endearingly neurotic pop star client Ella in Disney&#x2019;s Freakier Friday and in Amy Wang&#x2019;s horror-comedy Slanted. She has also guest starred in Prime Video&#x2019;s critically acclaimed series The Boys as Countess Crow and has voiced characters in witty coming-of-age stories including Netflix&#x2019;s Big Mouth and Disney&#x2019;s Turning Red . Up next, she has roles in The Angry Birds Movie 3 , in theaters Dec. 23, and season two of Prime Video&#x2019;s Legally Blonde prequel series Elle , expected to release next year.

Barone is a comedian, writer, actor and producer. She recently wrapped production on the independent film Still We Met , which Barone wrote and stars in opposite Joe Alwyn. Barone&#x2019;s original series Hard Feelings , which she created, wrote and will lead, was recently acquired by Hulu and A24. She also stars in and writes for the hit Amazon and A24 comedy series Overcompensating , which will return for a second season Feb. 17, 2027. Barone recently wrapped production on the Amazon MGM Studios romantic comedy Love Love , in which she will appear opposite Tyriq Withers and Isabel May. Her hourlong comedy special, Galaxy Brain , was released on Netflix in July 2026 and made the Netflix Top 10 the week of its release. Galaxy Brain was also released as a comedy album on Aug. 19 and as a limited edition vinyl this fall via Universal Music&#x2019;s MCA. Barone is the co-host of the popular podcast Ride with Benito Skinner. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-thr-article-mid-articleX-uid4' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setLazyLoadMultiplier(2) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Attended by 600 industry leaders and VIPs, THR &#x2019;s Women in Entertainment breakfast coincides with the release of The Hollywood Reporter &#x2019;s Women in Entertainment issue, featuring the highly anticipated Power 100, a list of the most powerful female executives and talent in entertainment.

Approximately 40 high school juniors and seniors currently participating in THR &#x2019;s Women in Entertainment Mentorship Program will attend the event. The program pairs some of the brightest young women from underserved high schools across Los Angeles with some of the most powerful female executives in film and TV. The WIE Mentorship Program, now in its 17th year, is a joint venture with Big Brothers Big Sisters of Greater Los Angeles and the Entertainment Industry Foundation. Over 300 students have taken part in the program, with mentees having received more than $16 million in scholarships over the past 17 years. A highlight of the annual breakfast, this year&#x2019;s celebration will feature the presentation of more than $500,000 in university scholarships to high school seniors in the program, generously provided by The Chuck Lorre Family Foundation and Lifetime. Earlier this month, The Hollywood Reporter announced Target as the new leading partner of its Women in Entertainment Mentorship Program.

Presented by founding sponsor Lifetime and title sponsor Lilly, THR &#x2019;s Women in Entertainment event is also sponsored by Delta Air Lines, Target, Waymo and WME and in partnership with Big Brothers Big Sisters of Greater Los Angeles, Entertainment Industry Foundation, Chapman University, Loyola Marymount University, Golden Goose, UTA Foundation and Warner Bros. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-thr-article-mid-articleX-uid5' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setLazyLoadMultiplier(2) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

The news comes on the heels of THR&#x2019;s Daytime Emmys win last month. THR&#x2019;s acclaimed video roundtable series, Off Script With The Hollywood Reporter , won the award for best arts and popular culture program.

Also in 2026, THR took home a record 20 SoCal Journalism Awards, including best magazine, best website and best podcast &#x2014; more wins than any other media outlet. It earned a record 96 nominations at the National Arts & Entertainment Journalism Awards, outpacing any other press organization, after winning 50 top honors in 2025. Other accolades include an American Society of Magazine Editors award for best cover and the 2026 Webby People&#x2019;s Voice Award for best entertainment website.

Banff World Media Festival executive director Jenn Kuzmyk is exiting after nine years in charge of the event, as well as her role as senior VP and publisher of Playback. Kuzmyk will depart both roles next month, but continue in a short-term consulting role with Brunico Communications with help with the transition.

A permanent replacement has not been named for Kuzmyk; instead, in the interim, Brunico president and CEO Russell Goldstein will oversee the commercial aspects of next year's Banff festival while Brunico chief content officer Mary Maddever will handle the event's programming. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories ‘Virgin River’ Renewed for Season 9 to Become Netflix’s Longest-Running Original Scripted Series Anthony Boyle on Becoming Sam Bankman-Fried for ‘The Altruists’ and Finding the Grey in History’s Villains: ‘I’ve Played More Real People Than Not’

Kuzmyk helped grow Banff into a popular international media festival, establishing new features such as Showrunner Superpanel and the Summit Series Keynotes, as well as the "Country of Honour" program. Industry heavyhitters who attended under her watch included Jeffrey Katzenberg, Ted Sarandos, Pearlena Igbokwe, Jesse Armstrong, George Cheeks, Channing Dungey and Rob Wade. Countries honored included South Korea in 2025 and Spain in 2026.

Also under Kuzmyk, Banff attracted attendees from all over the world, who also participated in the annual Rockie Awards.

&#x201C;Jenn&#x2019;s vision and passion have left an indelible mark on both Banff and Playback,&#x201D; Goldstein said in a statement. &#x201C;Under her watch, she has elevated these iconic brands with a consummate blend of strategic leadership and innovation. Building on this exceptional foundation, Banff 2027 is poised for growth under the stewardship of our remarkably talented and dedicated team. We are deeply grateful for Jenn&#x2019;s contributions and wish her every success in her next chapter.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Added Bell Media president Sean Cohan: &#x201C;On behalf of the Foundation Board of Directors, I want to extend our deepest gratitude to Jenn for her transformative leadership and unwavering commitment to both the Canadian and global screen-based industries. Over the past nine years, she has steered Banff through an era of rapid industry evolution with grace, foresight, and integrity, expanding its international reach while creating vital, career-defining opportunities for industry participants at every level. We thank her for her tremendous service and look forward to seeing all that she accomplishes next.&#x201D;

Kuzmyk also helped create programs such as Netflix-Banff Diversity of Voices Initiative, the Banff Spark Accelerator for Women in the Business of Media with Paramount+ and the Indigenous Screen Summit.

As head of Canadian industry trade Playback, Kuzmyk helped grow the publication's subscriber and advertising revenue.

"Leading Banff and Playback has been the privilege of my career," said Kuzmyk in a statement. "I want to thank Sean and the Banff board of directors for their trust, guidance and commitment to the festival, and our supporters, partners and sponsors, whose belief in Banff makes everything we do possible. To the Banff and Playback teams: you are the reason the festival and publication are as strong as they have ever been, and it has been a joy to work alongside you. I'm especially grateful to Russell Goldstein for his years of support and partnership. I leave knowing both Banff and Playback have never been in better shape, and I&#x2019;ll share more about what&#x2019;s next in the New Year for me.&#x201D;

Luca Guadagnino apologized to costume designers at the Marrakech Film Festival on Wednesday, a year after drawing backlash for comments he made about his preference for working with fashion designers on his films. However, the Italian filmmaker doubled down on his admiration for his frequent collaborator Jonathan Anderson, who most recently designed the costumes for his upcoming Silicon Valley drama &#x201C; Artificial .&#x201D;

&#x201C;I apologize to costume designers,&#x201D; Guadagnino said during a conversation at the festival. &#x201C;There are so many amazing costume designers that I admire so greatly through the history of cinema and contemporary history.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Elon Musk Criticizes Jeremy Culhane’s ‘SNL’ Impression: ‘They Need to Try Harder’ Inde Navarrette's 'SNL' Episode Hits Season High of 5.2 Million Viewers

The controversy dates back to last November, when Guadagnino, speaking with fashion journalist Tim Blanks at the Business of Fashion's annual VOICES conference, suggested that traditional costume designers were more concerned with the garments themselves than the bodies inhabiting them.

His comments drew the ire of several prominent costume designers, including Oscar winners Jenny Beavan (&#x201C;Mad Max: Fury Road,&#x201D; &#x201C;Cruella&#x201D;) and Kate Hawley (&#x201C;Frankenstein&#x201D;), who took to the comments section of Business of Fashion's Instagram post to dispute his characterization of their craft. Beavan wrote at the time, &#x201C;I can only add I am thankful he will never want to work with me!&#x201D;

In Marrakech, Guadagnino further explained his stance. &#x201C;It's just that I like to be in conversation with people who have an immediate touch with the pulse of how we live,&#x201D; he said.

Guadagnino singled out Anderson, who, in addition to serving as creative director of Dior, has designed the costumes for three of the filmmaker's movies: &#x201C;Challengers,&#x201D; &#x201C;Queer&#x201D; and &#x201C;Artificial.&#x201D; &#x201C;I know he's someone who sees life in front of him and cares about it,&#x201D; Guadagnino said of Anderson. &#x201C;It doesn't deal with fashion, per se.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

The pair's latest collaboration, &#x201C;Artificial,&#x201D; chronicles the rise of OpenAI and the dramatic ousting and subsequent reinstatement of its CEO Sam Altman in November 2023. The film stars Andrew Garfield as Altman, Yura Borisov as OpenAI co-founder Ilya Sutskever and Ike Barinholtz as Elon Musk.

&#x201C;I cannot think of anything more far from an idea of fashion or sophistication or form than Silicon Valley and tech bros,&#x201D; Guadagnino said. &#x201C;They actually are gross the way they present themselves.&#x201D;

The filmmaker went on to examine how the sartorial codes of the tech industry reflect a broader shift in how the world's wealthiest and most powerful people communicate their status. "[Anderson] was so smart in understanding every one of these characters and truly never had the temptation of painting something in a better color," Guadagnino said.

&#x201C;I believe that's also a language of power,&#x201D; he continued. &#x201C;The flip-flops of Zuckerberg are a comfortable item he wears, but also a way for him to indicate his position toward your position.&#x201D;

&#x201C;Artificial,&#x201D; which had its world premiere at the New York Film Festival in October, will screen at Marrakech Film Festival on Nov. 26. The film will be released by Neon in select theaters on Christmas Day before expanding nationwide on Jan. 8.

&nbsp; Share on X (Opens in new window) X Share on Facebook (Opens in new window) Facebook Add Us On Google Hugh Jackman’s best-known role is, without a doubt, Wolverine in the X-Men franchise. He played the role for almost two decades, starting with X-Men in 2000, with the latest appearance in 2024’s Deadpool & Wolverine. Recently, Jackman, along with Deadpool & Wolverine co-star Ryan Reynolds, has been added to the credits for Avengers: Doomsday for contributing literary material . Contributing material doesn’t mean they’ll be in the film, but given the X-Men co-stars reprising their roles in Doomsday , fans aren’t crossing out a surprise appearance from Jackman just yet.&nbsp;

As we wait to see whether Hugh Jackman’s denial of being in Avengers: Doomsday holds, it’s worth revisiting all the times he’s supposedly left the role. It’s probably a lesser amount of time than you think. Jackman has played Wolverine across eleven films, and unlike his castmates in X-Men , he continued his role through solo projects, with him happy to stay on as projects presented themselves. As long as the projects were compelling and did well, of course.&nbsp;

Like the larger X-Men film franchise, the Wolverine solo films are a mixed bag. There’s the high of Logan and the low of X-Men Origins: Wolverine. Although he didn’t express the sentiment publicly, the poor reception to X-Men Origins: Wolverine in 2009 seriously made Hugh Jackman reconsider his role. With X-Men Origins serving as a prequel, Jackman couldn’t see what the next film was going to be, and he wasn’t sure what else to do with the character.&nbsp;

Thankfully, Jackman had conversations with Darren Aronofsky, the initial director of The Wolverine before James Mangold took control of the project. Aronofsky stressed an alternative take on Wolverine’s ability to heal — just because Wolverine had healing powers that didn’t mean he didn’t have scars that would stay with him. Wolverine might have scars for a good 10 or 15 years before they faded. It gave Hugh Jackman a new approach to the character and a new outlook going forward. Four years later, the fruits of the approach would reach viewers with the release of The Wolverine in 2013.&nbsp;

In 2015, Hugh Jackman attended San Diego Comic-Con for an announcement. He thanked his fans for their love and support of the character, but doubled down on his promise that the next Wolverine film would be his “last time putting on the claws”. During the announcement, he teased his age, calling himself “Old Man Logan”, which, in hindsight, was a clear foreshadowing of the aging up of the character for Logan.

At the same time as declaring what would become Logan as his last project as Wolverine, Jackman held the door open for him to come back if Wolverine were to be allowed into the Marvel Cinematic Universe . Jackman said he’d “love to mix it up with Robert Downey Jr. and Iron Man and kick his ass.” It’s worth noting that Kevin Feige was an associate producer on X-Men , and Jackman kept up a positive working relationship with him over the years. The film Logan came out in 2017.&nbsp;

When Logan came out in 2017, Hugh Jackman wasn’t lying about being done with the role. He genuinely believed it. Jackman figured 17 years as Wolverine was enough and confirmed it was his last time in the role in interviews, citing advice from Jerry Seinfeld on knowing when it was best to end. A post to Hugh Jackman’s Instagram read “WOLVERINE… ONE LAST TIME.”

Even a call from Ryan Reynolds wasn’t enough to sway him. In January of 2017, Reynolds proposed a Deadpool Wolverine team-up film, but Jackman turned it down. He could see the merit in the project, but he felt that “the timing may be wrong.” At the time, Jackman felt he would’ve jumped on the film if it had come ten or so years earlier, but at the time, he felt that Deadpool didn’t need him. Of course, Jackman would later go back on his decision.&nbsp;

Hugh Jackman made another Instagram post in July of 2021. He posted an image of Wolverine’s arms and claws along with a poster of himself with Kevin Feige, current head of Marvel Studios. Of course, this set off speculation that Hugh Jackman would be reprising his role as Wolverine and thus bring the character into the MCU, a prospect Jackman had been excited about in the past. Later, Jackman would deny the rumors, citing that the first image he shared was fan art and it hadn’t occurred to him fans would assume otherwise and that it would “break the internet”.&nbsp;

III ✊ pic.twitter.com/ilSJFkOiVj

Press for Deadpool & Wolverine confirmed however it was only a year later that Jackman changed his mind about returning to the role. In 2022, he got a gut feeling that it was time to do the film and he called Ryan Reynolds on the phone, giving him the go-ahead. Reynolds got a call before Jackman’s own agent about committing to the film. During an appearance on Graham Norton — where Jackman had proclaimed being done with Wolverine back in 2015 — Jackman revealed that when on talk shows, he had to say “Nope, I’m not doing that again” even as he kept making another one. Jackman alluded to a changed philosophy and that he’s never saying “never” again.&nbsp;

While Jackman hasn’t exactly said "never" since, he has vehemently denied being in Avengers: Doomsday. When asked about Avengers: Secret Wars , Jackman repeated that he had no idea what the person was talking about . He then, in jest, joked that he had a chip in his brain that would shut him down if he said the wrong thing. Jackman may also joke about being the character until he’s 90 — a riff on a joke made during Deadpool & Wolverine — but fans have yet to see evidence for whether or not that’s true.&nbsp;

Do you believe Hugh Jackman’s done with Wolverine for the moment? Is he going to appear in Avengers: Doomsday or Secret Wars ? Let us know in the comment below!

